Hi Julian,

The PCA is calculated from the matrix of per-base methylation percentage over the samples (here is the code https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/master/R/clusterSamples.R#L401-L441).
The methylBase object that you describe contains information for each sample about the numbers of methylated (numCsX) and unmethylated (numTsX), which are required for the differential methylation testing.

Best,
Alex

